          "name": "Target",
          "type": "FNetAnalyticsAggregator*"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Data",
          "type": "TNetAnalyticsDataRef<>"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Data Name",
          "type": "Name&"
        },
        {
          "name": "In Type Name",
          "type": "String"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TNetAnalyticsDataPtr<>",
      "docs": "Use REGISTER_NET_ANALYTICS instead. Internal function, which registers a net analytics data holder, with an associated key name,\nand does type checking to ensure there have been no mixups with the data holder type.\nNOTE: May return nullptr! Analytics can be selectively enabled/disabled, based on the specified analytics data name.\n@param InData\t\tThe analytics data shared reference to be registered\n@param InDataName\tThe name given for referencing the analytics data\n@param InTypeName\tCompile-time derived type name for the analytics data - for type checking\n@return\t\t\t\tReturns the newly added analytics data shared reference"
    },
